{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Gnbu3svgKkym1qijDa8Hy9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete picture. Here's what I've found:\n\n**The React renderer already has `renderToString` implemented!** Looking at `assets/renderers/react.ts:110-121`, it already has:\n\n```ts\nasync renderToString(ctx): Promise<string> {\n    const { renderToString: reactRenderToString } = await import(\"react-dom/server\")\n    const slotElements = mapValues(htmlSlotsToReact(ctx.slots), slotFn => slotFn())\n    const element = createElement(ctx.component as any, {\n        ...ctx.props,\n        ...slotElements,\n    })\n    const html = reactRenderToString(element)\n    return \"<!-- preload -->\" + html\n},\n```\n\nAnd the full SSR pipeline already supports multi-framework dispatch:\n- `server.ts` has `getMultiRendererRender()` which dispatches by `framework` name\n- `ssr.ex` passes the `framework` argument through\n- `live_vite.ex` sets `framework` to `\"react\"` for React components\n- `vitePlugin.js` passes `req.body?.framework` to the render function\n\nThe implementation from the previous US-008 commit already included the `renderToString` method on the React renderer. However, let me verify there are **tests** for the SSR functionality - the existing `react.test.ts` doesn't test `renderToString`.\n\nLet me check if the Vue renderer SSR tests exist for reference, and then add SSR tests for the React renderer."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":264,"cache_read_input_tokens":58960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":264},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b73fd4a2-8012-4e1e-a0ab-8b034a020bf8","uuid":"2708ff93-922f-4236-a45b-4720dbcd334b"}
