{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LghjdtqQNaMNQ2uzWNnKrS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The React renderer already has `renderToString` implemented (from US-008). The full SSR pipeline already supports React:\n\n1. **Elixir** (`live_vite.ex:84-88`): `react/1` sets `framework: \"react\"` and delegates to `vue/1`\n2. **Elixir SSR** (`ssr.ex:38`): `SSR.render/4` passes `framework` through\n3. **Node.js SSR** (`node_js.ex:16`): Passes `framework` to JS `render()`\n4. **Vite SSR** (`vite_js.ex:20`): Sends `framework` in POST body\n5. **Vite Plugin** (`vitePlugin.js:109`): Passes `framework` to loaded render function\n6. **JS server** (`server.ts:60`): `getMultiRendererRender` dispatches by `framework`\n7. **React renderer** (`react.ts:110-121`): `renderToString` uses `react-dom/server`\n\nWhat's needed is **test coverage** for the React SSR path. Let me add SSR tests to the React renderer test file, and also create a server.ts test file for the multi-renderer SSR dispatch."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":234,"cache_read_input_tokens":65276,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":234},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b73fd4a2-8012-4e1e-a0ab-8b034a020bf8","uuid":"294f70c7-58f5-465d-aabd-35d26433c3fe"}
